 "bio": {
  "summary": {
   "text": "Shu Yun was the ancient khan of the Jeskai and a ghostfire warrior, known for convening a summit of the khans and giving his life to Ojutai to spare his clan.",
   "cites": [
    "khanfall-2015-02-18-r0",
    "khanfall-2015-02-18-e12"
   ],
   "links": [
    "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=The%20khan%20of%20the%20Jeskai%20fell.",
    "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=The%20khan%20of%20the%20Jeskai%20fell."
   ]
  },
  "bio": [
   {
    "text": "Shu Yun dictated a history of Tarkir at Dirgur and prepared to receive the arriving khans at his unprecedented summit.",
    "cites": [
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e0"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=This%20meeting%2C%20this%20council,the%20odds%20of%20survival."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "He halted the khans' quarrels, urged them to stand together against the dragons, and insisted on balance and on seeking Ugin when they disagreed over the cocoon and the brood-lords.",
    "cites": [
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e2",
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e6"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=We%20must%20stand%20together%2C,vanish%20from%20the%20world.",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=The%20destruction%20of%20the,destruction%20of%20the%20clans."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "When the dragon broods flew toward Dirgur and the khans realized the summit had been leaked, Alesha suspected Shu Yun, who denied it.",
    "cites": [
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e7",
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e8"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=Out%20over%20the%20water%2C,other%2C%20crashed%20together%E2%80%A6and%20merged",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=Someone%20must%20have%20told,little%20summit%2C%22%20said%20Reyhan."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "He took the Annals scrolls from his scribe Quan, leapt from the window onto Silumgar's dragon and killed it with his tattooed palm, then hid the scroll case beneath the stronghold and swallowed the key.",
    "cites": [
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e10",
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e11",
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-r1"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=His%20dragon%20tattoo%20flashed,on%20the%20dragon%27s%20skull.",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=He%20shut%20the%20door%2C,back%20to%20the%20courtyard.",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=Shu%20Yun%20turned%20to,most%20trusted%20scribe%2C%20Quan."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Shu Yun then knelt before Ojutai and offered his life to spare the Jeskai, and Ojutai froze him to death.",
    "cites": [
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-e12",
     "khanfall-2015-02-18-r2"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=The%20khan%20of%20the%20Jeskai%20fell.",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/khanfall-2015-02-18#:~:text=Ojutai%27s%20jaws%20opened%2C%20and,end%20of%20the%20world."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Later accounts recall that his bargain meant all ghostfire warriors would die to spare the rest of the Jeskai, though Tae Jin's mother, a scribe of Shu Yun, survived Ojutai's purge.",
    "cites": [
     "chronicle-bolas-things-unseen-2018-06-27-e20",
     "chronicle-bolas-whispers-treachery-2018-07-11-e1"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-things-unseen-2018-06-27#:~:text=You%20wear%20the%20dragon,of%20a%20ghostfire%20warrior.",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-whispers-treachery-2018-07-11#:~:text=She%20survived%20Ojutai%27s%20purge,of%20the%20Jeskai%20Way."
    ]
   }
  ],
